    {
      "parameters": {
        "mode": "raw",
        "jsonOutput": "={\n  \"resume\": \"M RAKESH\\nLocation: Hyderabad, India\\n\\nPROFESSIONAL SUMMARY\\nComputer Science graduate (B.Tech 2026) and aspiring AI/ML & Generative AI Engineer with hands-on experience building machine learning, deep learning, computer vision, LLM and RAG applications. Skilled in Python, TensorFlow, Keras, LangChain, ChromaDB, OpenCV and Streamlit. Seeking entry-level roles in AI/ML, Generative AI and Python development.\\n\\nTECHNICAL SKILLS\\nLanguages: Python\\nMachine Learning & Deep Learning: TensorFlow, Keras, scikit-learn, CNNs, data augmentation, model evaluation (confusion matrix, ROC-AUC)\\nGenerative AI & LLM Engineering: LLMs, NLP & Transformers, RAG pipelines, Multimodal RAG, multi-query retrieval, LangChain, OpenAI API, CLIP, embeddings (Sentence-Transformers)\\nVector Databases & Data: ChromaDB, vector search, Pandas, PyMuPDF\\nComputer Vision: OpenCV, Haar Cascades, image classification, image preprocessing\\nTools & Deployment: Streamlit, Git & GitHub, Jupyter, Google Colab, APIs, Automation (n8n)\\n\\nPROJECTS\\n1. PDF Lens - Multimodal RAG System (deployed, live demo)\\nTech: Python, LangChain, CLIP, ChromaDB, GPT-4o-mini (Vision), Streamlit\\n- Users upload any PDF and ask questions in plain English; answers use text, images and charts and cite page numbers.\\n- Extracted text, images and charts with PyMuPDF; detected charts using CLIP zero-shot classification; embedded text (all-MiniLM-L6-v2) and images (CLIP) into two ChromaDB collections.\\n- Implemented multi-query retrieval so different wording still finds the right content; a vision LLM explains charts and states clearly when information is missing.\\n\\n2. SmartPDF Chat - RAG Document Assistant\\nTech: Python, LangChain, ChromaDB, Sentence-Transformers, OpenAI\\n- PDF question-answering assistant using Retrieval-Augmented Generation with an interactive chat loop.\\n- Split documents into 1000-character chunks (200 overlap), embedded them and stored vectors in persistent ChromaDB.\\n- Retrieved top-k relevant chunks and prompted the LLM to answer only from document context, reducing hallucinations.\\n\\n3. Real vs AI-Generated Face Detection\\nTech: Python, TensorFlow, Keras, CNN, OpenCV, Google Colab\\n- Trained a CNN classifier to distinguish real photos from AI-generated images on 7,408 images, reaching 99.14% test accuracy.\\n- Used data augmentation, EarlyStopping and ReduceLROnPlateau to limit overfitting; evaluated with confusion matrix, classification report and ROC-AUC; added OpenCV Haar Cascade face detection.\\n\\n4. AI Job Hunt Assistant (n8n automation)\\nTech: n8n, OpenAI API, JSearch API, Google Sheets, Telegram Bot\\n- Built an automated workflow that fetches daily job postings, scores each against my resume with an LLM, writes tailored cover letters and sends top matches to Telegram with interactive buttons.\\n\\nEDUCATION\\nB.Tech - Computer Science Engineering, CGPA 8.1 (2022 - 2026)\\nKommuri Pratap Reddy Institute of Technology (KPRIT), Hyderabad\\n\\nCERTIFICATIONS\\n100 Days of Code: The Complete Python Bootcamp\\n\\nEXPERIENCE LEVEL\\nFresher / entry-level (0-1 years)\",\n  \"targetRoles\": \"AI Engineer, Machine Learning Engineer, Generative AI Engineer, AI/ML Intern, Associate Software Engineer, Associate Data Scientist, Associate AI Engineer, Graduate Engineer Trainee (software/IT), Software Engineer Trainee, Programmer Analyst Trainee, Python Developer, Junior Data Scientist, Data Analyst\",\n  \"preferredLocations\": \"Hyderabad (strongly preferred), Remote (acceptable)\",\n  \"telegramChatId\": \"YOUR_TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID\",\n  \"searchQueries\": \"AI engineer in Hyderabad, India | machine learning engineer in Hyderabad, India | python developer in Hyderabad, India | associate software engineer in Hyderabad, India | graduate engineer trainee in Hyderabad, India | data scientist in Hyderabad, India\",\n  \"minScore\": 55,\n  \"topN\": 5,\n  \"maxJobsPerRun\": 30,\n  \"testMode\": False\n}",
        "options": {
          "dotNotation": false
        }
      },
      "id": "1247b5e1-50db-41c1-9cc2-a863ba8a51b4",
      "name": "Config",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.set",
      "typeVersion": 3.5,
      "position": [
        224,
        208
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "const hash = (s) => {\n  let h = 5381;\n  for (const ch of s) h = ((h * 33) ^ ch.charCodeAt(0)) >>> 0;\n  return h.toString(36);\n};\n\nconst seen = new Set();\nconst out = [];\n\nfor (const item of $input.all()) {\n  const j = item.json;\n  const title = String(j.title || '').trim();\n  const company = String(j.company || '').trim();\n  if (!title) continue;\n\n  const jobId = 'j' + hash((title + '|' + company).toLowerCase());\n  if (seen.has(jobId)) continue;\n  seen.add(jobId);\n\n  out.push({\n    json: {\n      jobId,\n      title,\n      company,\n      location: String(j.location || '').trim(),\n      link: String(j.link || '').trim(),\n      source: String(j.source || '').trim(),\n      details: String(j.details || '').trim(),\n    },\n  });\n}\n\nreturn out;"
      },
      "id": "273a03bb-ef1c-4a5b-8e0f-e8405349f6a9",
      "name": "Normalize Jobs",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
